```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <regex>
#include <thread>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    std::string html = markdown;
    std::regex re(R"(^|\s*)\*(.*)");
    std::regex_replace(html, re, R"$1<b>$2</b>");
    return html;
}

void main() {
    std::string markdown = "This is a *sample* of markdown text.";
    std::string html = markdownToHtml(markdown);
    std::cout << html << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This function uses a regular expression to replace markdown asterisks (`*`) with HTML bold tags (`<b>`). The regular expression `R"(^|\s*)\*(.*)"` matches an asterisk followed by zero or more characters at the start or end of the string, and captures the asterisk followed by its content. The `std::regex_replace` function is used to replace the asterisks with HTML bold tags.

The `main` function demonstrates how to use the `markdownToHtml` function to convert a markdown string to HTML.

